 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "communityToFollowers[i] lists the distinct follower ids \"F<j>\" following community \"C<i>\", and followerToCommunities[j] lists the distinct community ids \"C<i>\" followed by \"F<j>\"; the two lists describe the same relation (F<j> is in communityToFollowers[i] exactly when C<i> is in followerToCommunities[j]) and ids are written without leading zeros. If communityIdx is outside [0, communityToFollowers.length) or community communityIdx has no followers, return []. Level 2 (inferred extension): return every community other than communityIdx that is connected to it through a chain of shared followers (C<a> and C<b> are linked when some follower follows both; take the transitive closure), as ids \"C<i>\" ordered by increasing i.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
